<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44283" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silvātĭcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sylv-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a wood</i>
			or <i>to trees</i>, <i>wood-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 11, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 22,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of plants and animals, <i>growing</i> or <i>running wild</i>,
				<i>wild</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurus, mala, pirus. etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 8, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">143, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pirus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 40, 5</span></i>
			: sus, id. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 555, 31</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Aug. 8, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 8, 22, § 70</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
